-- title:
--   Special-fibre points of codimension ≤ 1 are ξ_∞ or ξ₀
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime not dividing $N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`: a structure bundling, for the map `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` from the level-$(N_0q)$ Igusa-type curve to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the base ring `DRLevel.R q`, properness, flatness, integrality of the source and local finite presentation, integral closedness of the sections over every affine open, together with a curve model of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ identified with the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and compatible with the Galois action and with the $q$-expansions of the finite-chart algebra, smoothness of relative dimension $1$ and geometric integrality of the fibre over $\mathbb Q$, sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ of the base map, and further data. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O\colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$; let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring homomorphism $O\to\kappa$. Write $X$ for `DRLevel.XO ρO`, the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$, with structural map `DRLevel.XO.toBase ρO` to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ given by the second projection. Then for every point $z$ of $X$ lying outside the preimage of the basic open $D(q)\subseteq\operatorname{Spec} O$, whose local ring has Krull dimension at most $1$, one has $z =$ `𝔛.ξinf ρO toκ` or $z =$ `𝔛.ξzero ρO toκ`, the two points of $X$ attached to the package.
--
--   This is the codimension statement for the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ base changed to a discrete valuation ring in which $q$ is a uniformiser: a point of the fibre over the closed point whose local ring has dimension at most one must be one of the two distinguished points $\xi_\infty,\xi_0$, so that every other special-fibre point has local dimension $\ge 2$. It is used in the codimension clause of the crossing-frame data [`V3AsmLevel.codim`](thm.html#V3AsmLevel.codim).
